    <statement><p>Find the differential of the function
<m>z = e^{x}\cos\mathopen{}\left(y\right)</m>.</p>
<p><m>dz =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>e^{x}\cos\mathopen{}\left(y\right)dx+-e^{x}\sin\mathopen{}\left(y\right)dy</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>z_x = e^{x}\cos\mathopen{}\left(y\right)</m> and <m>z_y = -e^{x}\sin\mathopen{}\left(y\right)</m>,
we have
<me>dz = e^{x}\cos\mathopen{}\left(y\right)dx+\left(-e^{x}\right)\sin\mathopen{}\left(y\right)dy.</me>



</solution>
